# Workshop branch naming

When proposing a branch name — including via Cursor's built-in **Create Branch & Commit** button — use the pattern:

```
workshop/<handle>-<short-feature>
```

- `<handle>` is the participant's GitHub handle or first name in lowercase.
- `<short-feature>` is 2–4 lowercase words separated by hyphens describing the change.

## Examples

- `workshop/jgrace-reset-zoom-button`
- `workshop/alice-stroke-palette-color`
- `workshop/bob-welcome-screen-copy`
- `workshop/cloud-agent-jsdoc-a1f` (cloud agent variant; see the `generate-cloud-agent-prompt` skill)

## Avoid

- Generic names like `feature`, `update`, `wip`, `branch1`, `cursor/...`.
- Names without the `workshop/` prefix — automations filter PRs by this prefix and will skip non-workshop branches.
- Slashes inside the suffix (the prefix `workshop/` is the only slash).

If a branch name has already been created without this prefix, rename it before pushing:

```
git branch -m <new-name>
```
